= Feedback — Technical =

== Closed-loop control ==
For plant G(s) and feedback path H(s), a standard negative-feedback transfer function is:

<pre>
T(s) = G(s) / (1 + G(s)H(s))
</pre>

under conventional sign definitions.

== Dynamics ==
Feedback changes system dynamics, not just static gain.

Stability depends on loop gain, poles, zeros, delays, nonlinearities, saturation, and disturbances.

== Cybernetic scope ==
Cybernetics generalized feedback beyond engineering to biological, cognitive, and social systems.

That broader analogy is useful only when a real causal loop is identified.

